{"abstract":"Most research on implicit discourse relation identification has focused on written language, however, it is also crucial to understand these relations in spoken discourse. We introduce a novel method for implicit discourse relation identification across both text and speech, that allows us to extract examples of semantically equivalent pairs of implicit and explicit discourse markers, based on aligning speech+transcripts with subtitles in another language variant. We apply our method to Egyptian Arabic, resulting in a novel high-quality dataset of spoken implicit discourse relations. We present a comprehensive approach to modeling implicit discourse relation classification using audio and text data with a range of different models. We find that text-based models outperform audio-based models, but combining text and audio features can lead to enhanced performance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ruby, Ahmed","Hardmeier, Christian","Stymne, Sara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828151"],"event":{"acronym":"COLING","title":"International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Implicit discourse relations","Multimodal discourse analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimodal extraction and recognition of arabic implicit discourse relations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.363.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828151","identifier":[{"id":"85218500872","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5700370f-231a-4838-b40a-3d59658a01d0"],"keyword":["Egyptian Arabic dataset","Implicit discourse relations","Multimodal discourse analysis","Spoken language processing","Text and audio fusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-56E7627238AC881912A2F827234AF3E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.363.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmed","key":"rubypau","last":"Ruby","name":"Ruby, Ahmed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"stymnepau","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"5425-5429","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics (COLING)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5700370f-231a-4838-b40a-3d59658a01d0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multimodal Extraction and Recognition of Arabic Implicit Discourse Relations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828151","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Reliable automatic solutions to extract structured information from free-text nursing notes could bring important efficiency gains in healthcare, but their development is hampered by the sensitivity and limited availability of example data. We describe a method for eliciting fictitious nursing documentation and associated structured documentation from volunteers and a resulting dataset of 397 Danish notes collected and annotated through a custom web application from 98 participating nurses. After some manual refinement, we obtained a high-quality dataset containing nurse notes with relevant entities identified. We describe the implementation and limitations of our approach as well as initial experiments in a named entity tagging setup.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bornerup, Jesper Vaaben","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828171"],"event":{"acronym":"NODALIDA","title":"Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nursing documentation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient elicitation of fictitious nursing notes from volunteer healthcare professionals","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/10062/107267","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828171","ids":["itu-ab083361-027d-41a4-893d-202dbcc9b853"],"keyword":["Automatic information extraction","Fictitious data generation","Named entity tagging","Nursing documentation","Sensitive data challenges"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C7034A675AF81B03AAA8BABD278DFDAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/10062/107267","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Vaaben","key":"borneruppau","last":"Bornerup","name":"Bornerup, Jesper Vaaben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"739-754","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Joint 25th Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics and 11th Baltic Conference on Human Language Technologies (NoDaLiDa/Baltic-HLT)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ab083361-027d-41a4-893d-202dbcc9b853"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficient Elicitation of Fictitious Nursing Notes from Volunteer Healthcare Professionals","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828171","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Multilingual phone recognition models can learn language-independent pronunciation patterns from large volumes of spoken data and recognize them across languages. This potential can be harnessed to improve speech technologies for underresourced languages. However, these models are typically trained on phonological representations of speech sounds, which do not necessarily reflect the phonetic realization of speech. A mismatch between a phonological symbol and its phonetic realizations can lead to phone confusions and reduce performance. This work introduces formant-based vowel categorization aimed at improving cross-lingual vowel recognition by uncovering a vowel's phonetic quality from its formant frequencies, and reorganizing the vowel categories in a multilingual speech corpus to increase their consistency across languages. The work investigates vowel categories obtained from a trilingual multi-dialect speech corpus of Danish, Norwegian, and Swedish using three categorization techniques. Cross-lingual phone recognition experiments reveal that uniting vowel categories of different languages into a set of shared formant-based categories improves cross-lingual recognition of the shared vowels, but also interferes with recognition of vowels not present in one or more training languages. Cross-lingual evaluation on regional dialects provides inconclusive results. Nevertheless, improved recognition of individual vowels can translate to improvements in overall phone recognition on languages unseen during training.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stepanovic, Marija","Hardmeier, Christian","Scharenborg, Odette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828139"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"keyword":["Consonants","Phonetics","Phonology","Speech communication","Speech production","Speech sounds","Vocalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formant based vowel categorization for cross lingual phone recognition","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0036222","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828139","identifier":[{"id":"105001235132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-12ef8a63-313d-4de7-aa6b-9d7bdf775946"],"keyword":["Consonants","Covariance and correlation","Human voice","Phonetics","Phonology","Speech communication","Speech production","Speech sounds","Vocalization","Vowel systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-73E5C15772ED7F663171FEB8C895B34D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0036222","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Odette","key":"scharenborgpau","last":"Scharenborg","name":"Scharenborg, Odette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-12ef8a63-313d-4de7-aa6b-9d7bdf775946"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formant-Based Vowel Categorization for Cross-Lingual Phone Recognition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828139","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Dehumanization is a mental process that enables the exclusion and ill treatment of a group of people. In this paper, we present two data sets of dehumanizing text, a large, automatically collected corpus and a smaller, manually annotated data set. Both data sets include a combination of political discourse and dialogue from movie subtitles. Our methods give us a broad and varied amount of dehumanization data to work with, enabling further exploratory analysis and automatic classification of dehumanization patterns","author_count":3,"contributors":["Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","Hardmeier, Christian","Engelmann, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776448"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated text classification","Dehumanization","Political discourse"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a dataset for the detection of dehumanizing language","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2402.08764","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-776448","identifier":[{"id":"85185868622","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c105cfde-646f-401f-a0d8-d78c7c415acb"],"keyword":["Automated text classification","Dehumanization","Movie subtitles","Political discourse","Text corpora"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3E965E2F5944EB048A1A752FE5D52020"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2402.08764","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brunsgaard","key":"trollepau","last":"Trolle","locid":"d21db1f2-9a89-4611-8077-e06e89985faa","name":"Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"engelmannpau","last":"Engelmann","name":"Engelmann, Paul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c105cfde-646f-401f-a0d8-d78c7c415acb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Dataset for the Detection of Dehumanizing Language","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776448","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We investigate whether prosody can help to disambiguate discourse relations. To address this question, we conducted a controlled experiment examining the impact of prosody in the absence of context, which is crucial for disambiguation. The aim was to determine whether specific prosodic features correlate with the disambiguation of implicit discourse relations. The dataset used in the experiment consisted of 22 pairs of examples, recorded by 21 native speakers of Egyptian Arabic. These examples are two-part sentences with an implicit discourse relation that can be ambiguously read as either causal or concessive, paired with two different preceding context sentences forcing either the causal or the concessive reading. We use linear mixed-effects models to analyze the impact of causal versus concessive discourse relations on prosodic features. We find that, relative to the causal relation, the concessive relation was produced with a longer pause duration between discourse segments, a wider F0 interquartile range for the second segment, and a lower last F0 max for the first segment. These differences are statistically significant, suggesting that speakers use prosody to distinguish between causal and concessive relations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ruby, Ahmed","Hardmeier, Christian","Stymne, Sara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828184"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Implicit discourse relations","Prosody"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating the role of prosody in disambiguating implicit discourse relations in egyptian arabic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21437/SpeechProsody.2024-187","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828184","identifier":[{"id":"105008057033","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ee9d1257-61f4-48ad-92a3-d3fdddd8cebb"],"keyword":["Causal-concessive disambiguation","Egyptian Arabic","Fundamental frequency variation","Implicit discourse relations","Prosody"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7395B3242D29E46417E196E88DE06D07"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.isca-archive.org/speechprosody_2024/ruby24_speechprosody.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21437/SpeechProsody.2024-187","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmed","key":"rubypau","last":"Ruby","name":"Ruby, Ahmed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"stymnepau","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21437/speechprosody.2024-187","pages":"926-930","publisher":"International Speech Communication Association (ISCA)","status":"p","title":"Speech Prosody 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008057033"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ee9d1257-61f4-48ad-92a3-d3fdddd8cebb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigating the Role of Prosody in Disambiguating Implicit Discourse Relations in Egyptian Arabic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828184","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","Hardmeier, Christian","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718860"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Content moderation","Dataset coherence","Hate speech"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safenet challenges and strategies in combatting online hate speech","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102473644/SafeNet_abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718860","ids":["itu-63d5d848-3210-4249-af8f-6e81ff8ca8c5"],"keyword":["Content moderation","Dataset coherence","Hate speech"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A5E12D62C637B4C53BA3D6F108F0B989"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102473656/SafeNet_poster.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102473644/SafeNet_abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brunsgaard","key":"trollepau","last":"Trolle","locid":"d21db1f2-9a89-4611-8077-e06e89985faa","name":"Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-63d5d848-3210-4249-af8f-6e81ff8ca8c5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SafeNet: Challenges and strategies in combatting online hate speech","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718860","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Most pronouns are referring expressions, computers need to resolve what do the pronouns refer to, and there are divergences on pronoun usage across languages. Thus, dealing with these divergences and translating pronouns is a challenge in machine translation. Mentions are referring candidates of pronouns and have closer relations with pronouns compared to general tokens. We assume that extracting additional mention features can help pronoun translation. Therefore, we introduce an additional mention attention module in the decoder to pay extra attention to source mentions but not non-mention tokens. Our mention attention module not only extracts features from source mentions, but also considers target-side context which benefits pronoun translation. In addition, we also introduce two mention classifiers to train models to recognize mentions, whose outputs guide the mention attention. We conduct experiments on the WMT17 English–German translation task, and evaluate our models on general translation and pronoun translation, using BLEU, APT, and contrastive evaluation metrics. Our proposed model outperforms the baseline Transformer model in terms of APT and BLEU scores, this confirms our hypothesis that we can improve pronoun translation by paying additional attention to source mentions, and shows that our introduced additional modules do not have negative effect on the general translation quality.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tang, Gongbo","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776443"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Language and Culture University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mention attention for pronoun translation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.14829","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-776443","identifier":[{"id":"85185883719","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b34f5987-c4ab-4ebc-89a6-1f31cf2f9709"],"keyword":["Mention attention","Pronoun translation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A091F99E2C8F4066A4FD253091360811"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.14829","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing language and culture university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Language and Culture University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gongbo","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Gongbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3632971.3632977","isbn":["9798400707704"],"pages":"161-164","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185883719"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b34f5987-c4ab-4ebc-89a6-1f31cf2f9709"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mention Attention for Pronoun Translation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776443","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
