{"abstract":"Coreference resolution is the task of finding expressions that refer to the same entity in a text. Coreference models are generally trained on monolingual annotated data but annotating coreference is expensive and challenging. Hardmeier et al. (2013) have shown that parallel data contains latent anaphoric knowledge, but it has not been explored in end-to-end neural models yet. In this paper, we propose a simple yet effective model to exploit coreference knowledge from parallel data. In addition to the conventional modules learning coreference from annotations, we introduce an unsupervised module to capture cross-lingual coreference knowledge. Our proposed cross-lingual model achieves consistent improvements, up to 1.74 percentage points, on the OntoNotes 5.0 English dataset using 9 different synthetic parallel datasets. These experimental results confirm that parallel data can provide additional coreference knowledge which is beneficial to coreference resolution tasks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tang, Gongbo","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712526"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Language and Culture University"],"keyword":["Anaphoric Knowledge","Coreference Knowledge","Coreference Resolution","Cross lingual Coreference","Monolingual Annotated Data","Neural models","OntoNotes 5 0","Parallel Data","Synthetic Datasets","Unsupervised learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parallel data helps neural entity coreference resolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712526","identifier":[{"id":"85175434823","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-669e4778-b4ea-49eb-a8dc-920fe5722925"],"keyword":["Anaphoric Knowledge","Coreference Knowledge","Coreference Resolution","Cross-lingual Coreference","Monolingual Annotated Data","Neural Models","OntoNotes 5.0","Parallel Data","Synthetic Datasets","Unsupervised Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-40BF75BD02D64A87F4441A1004CF7298"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.findings-acl.197.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing language and culture university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Language and Culture University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gongbo","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Gongbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"rogerspedh","last":"Rogers","name":"Rogers, Anna","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jordan","key":"boydgraberpedh","last":"Boyd-Graber","name":"Boyd-Graber, Jordan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naoaki","key":"okazakipedh","last":"Okazaki","name":"Okazaki, Naoaki","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","edition":"2023","eisbn":["9781959429623"],"pages":"3162-3171","place":"Canada","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-669e4778-b4ea-49eb-a8dc-920fe5722925"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parallel Data Helps Neural Entity Coreference Resolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712526","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present principles of constructing and resolving ambiguity in implicit discourse relations. Following these principles, we created a dataset in both English and Egyptian Arabic that controls for semantic disambiguation, enabling the investigation of prosodic features in future work. In these datasets, examples are two-part sentences with an implicit discourse relation that can be ambiguously read as either causal or concessive, paired with two different preceding context sentences forcing either the causal or the concessive reading. We also validated both datasets by humans and language models (LMs) to study whether context can help humans or LMs resolve ambiguities of implicit relations and identify the intended relation. As a result, this task posed no difficulty for humans, but proved challenging for BERT/CamelBERT and ELECTRA/AraELECTRA models.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ruby, Ahmed","Stymne, Sara","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712562"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Contextual ambiguity","Human vs language model validation","Implicit discourse relations","Prosodic features","Semantic disambiguation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unpacking ambiguous structure a dataset for ambiguous implicit discourse relations for english and egyptian arabic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.codi-1.16","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712562","identifier":[{"id":"85174831794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e6a099ef-98c8-4f2d-8e58-fca480c19af2"],"keyword":["Contextual ambiguity","Human vs. language model validation","Implicit discourse relations","Prosodic features","Semantic disambiguation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CD50E5011CF5B1F672CF1603A0AA1F61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.codi-1.16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.codi-1.16","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmed","key":"rubypau","last":"Ruby","name":"Ruby, Ahmed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"stymnepau","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.codi-1.16","eisbn":["9781959429890"],"pages":"126-144","place":"Canada","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 4th Workshop on Computational Approaches to Discourse (CODI 2023)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174831794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e6a099ef-98c8-4f2d-8e58-fca480c19af2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unpacking Ambiguous Structure: A Dataset for Ambiguous Implicit Discourse Relations for English and Egyptian Arabic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712562","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Popular approaches for quantifying predictive uncertainty in deep neural networks often involve distributions over weights or multiple models, for instance via Markov Chain sampling, ensembling, or Monte Carlo dropout. These techniques usually incur overhead by having to train multiple model instances or do not produce very diverse predictions. This comprehensive and extensive survey aims to familiarize the reader with an alternative class of models based on the concept of Evidential Deep Learning: For unfamiliar data, they aim to admit \"what they don't know\", and fall back onto a prior belief. Furthermore, they allow uncertainty estimation in a single model and forward pass by parameterizing distributions over distributions. This survey recapitulates existing works, focusing on the implementation in a classification setting, before surveying the application of the same paradigm to regression. We also reflect on the strengths and weaknesses compared to other existing methods and provide the most fundamental derivations using a unified notation to aid future research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis","Hardmeier, Christian","Frellsen, Jes"],"cuid":["S02-099.60-692198"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bayesian methods","Classification and Regression","Deep neural networks","Evidential Deep Learning","Markov Chain Sampling","Model Ensembling","Monte Carlo Dropout","Parameterizing Distributions","Predictive Uncertainty","Uncertainty Estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pioneer Centre for AI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prior and posterior networks a survey on evidential deep learning methods for uncertainty estimation","src":["dtu","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/330944105/720_prior_and_posterior_networks_a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.60-692198","identifier":[{"id":"105000052164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fc7a14e6-dbe9-4790-93ff-bee0314232c4","itu-c7f81896-c30d-4035-bf12-322f8099e025"],"keyword":["Bayesian Methods","Classification and Regression","Deep Neural Networks","Evidential Deep Learning","Markov Chain Sampling","Model Ensembling","Monte Carlo Dropout","Parameterizing Distributions","Predictive Uncertainty","Uncertainty Estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3735EBC3A7FBAA178530F907206EA82A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=xqS8k9E75c","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/330944105/720_prior_and_posterior_networks_a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://jmlr.org/tmlr","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://orbit.dtu.dk/files/330944105/720_prior_and_posterior_networks_a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pioneer Centre for AI"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jes","key":"frellsenpau","last":"Frellsen","locid":"6333536d-7de1-46f9-ad12-8c397d149c1a","name":"Frellsen, Jes","orcid":"0000-0001-9224-1271","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["28358856"],"journal":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000052164"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fc7a14e6-dbe9-4790-93ff-bee0314232c4","itu-c7f81896-c30d-4035-bf12-322f8099e025"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prior and Posterior Networks : A Survey on Evidential Deep Learning Methods For Uncertainty Estimation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskni