Predictive Uncertainty and Calibration in NLP: A Study on the Impact of Method &amp; Data Scarcity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384254","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The field of Deep Learning (DL) has undergone explosive growth during the last decade, with a substantial impact on Natural Language Processing (NLP) as well. Yet, as with other fields employing DL techniques, there has been a lack of common experimental standards compared to more established disciplines. Starting from fundamental scientific principles, we distill ongoing discussions on experimental standards in DL into a single, widely-applicable methodology. Following these best practices is crucial to strengthening experimental evidence, improve reproducibility and enable scientific progress. These standards are further collected in a public repository to help them transparently adapt to future needs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Bassignana, Elisa","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Varab, Daniel","Zhang, Mike","Hardmeier, Christian","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384979"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental standards for deep learning research a natural language processing perspective","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038600/2204.06251.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384979","ids":["itu-fc23a8ce-731e-4697-aad6-c6f8388c5a44"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6AB440FD4ABC40E82D47ECE926F352D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038600/2204.06251.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"varabpau","last":"Varab","name":"Varab, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fc23a8ce-731e-4697-aad6-c6f8388c5a44"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental Standards for Deep Learning Research: A Natural Language Processing Perspective","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384979","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Exploring aspects of sentential meaning that are implicit or underspecified in context is important for sentence understanding. In this paper, we propose a novel architecture based on mentions for revision requirements detection. The goal is to improve understandability, addressing some types of revisions, especially for the Replaced Pronoun type. We show that our mention-based system can predict replaced pronouns well on the mentionlevel. However, our combined sentence-level system does not improve on the sentence-level BERT baseline. We also present additional contrastive systems, and show results for each type of edit.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ruby, Ahmed","Hardmeier, Christian","Stymne, Sara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381553"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Contextual underspecification","Mention based architecture","Replaced Pronoun detection","Revision requirements detection","Sentential meaning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a mention based system for revision requirements detection","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422640/2021.unimplicit_1.7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381553","identifier":[{"id":"85138688635","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-130119f2-e6f5-4b18-a96b-6380f9261ac9"],"keyword":["Contextual underspecification","Mention-based architecture","Replaced Pronoun detection","Revision requirements detection","Sentential meaning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4988F806602BF07B9F72F3C0AFC76F0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2021.unimplicit-1.7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422640/2021.unimplicit_1.7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmed","key":"rubypau","last":"Ruby","name":"Ruby, Ahmed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"stymnepau","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"58-63","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the First Workshop on Understanding Implicit and Underspecified Language (UnImplicit)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-130119f2-e6f5-4b18-a96b-6380f9261ac9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A mention-based system for revision requirements detection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381553","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Accurate translation requires documentlevel information, which is ignored by sentence-level machine translation. Recent work has demonstrated that document-level consistency can be improved with automatic post-editing (APE) using only targetlanguage (TL) information. We study an extended APE model that additionally integrates source context. A human evaluation of fluency and adequacy in EnglishRussian translation reveals that the model with access to source context significantly outperforms monolingual APE in terms of adequacy, an effect largely ignored by automatic evaluation metrics. Our results show that TL-only modelling increases fluency without improving adequacy, demonstrating the need for conditioning on source text for automatic post-editing. They also highlight blind spots in automatic methods for targeted evaluation and demonstrate the need for human assessment to evaluate document-level translation quality reliably.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wang, Chaojun","Hardmeier, Christian","Sennrich, Rico"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384251"],"event":{"acronym":"NODALIDA","title":"Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh","University of Zurich","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["automatic post editing","document level translation","human evaluation methods","source context integration","translation adequacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the importance of source text in automatic post editing for context aware machine translation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"typ